__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
pytest-cache-files-*/
# The record root, whole: `.keel/review/` was narrowed to the export directory, so the default run
# record (`runs.jsonl`, and `review-context.json` beside it) showed up as untracked noise in every
# repository that ran `keelcheck gate run`. Records are the tool's own history, not source.
.keel/
# Scratch the lanes actually create inside the checked-out repo. Untracked paths count as dirt to a
# `git status --porcelain` check, so a scratch directory beside the code made `gate run` refuse to
# start: `.assay-tmp/` is Sift's probe root, and `.keel-*/` is the prefix the suite's own scratch
# helper uses (`.keel-test-tmp`, `.keel-write-probe-*`).
.assay-tmp/
.keel-*/
